  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-01-18T23:06:34.885Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The inclusion of groups and group instances has been great, and running a community with it has been very good. One thing that holds it back though is not being able to title these group instances. Like, what are the people doing in that instance? It'd be great to be able give it a name or a title.\n\nThe community I run does up to 2 dozen weekly events and we use the group function for many of them now, but we cannot use them for all of them because of this particular thing. If we have two events happening that overlap, only one can use it because you can't tell which is which. Any event with two instances being run, can't use it because again, can't tell which is which. \n\nI realize these are somewhat specific use cases, but I feel like it's a natural movement for the group instances for everyone. What's more likely to get people in your group to join? Just an instance of a world open with no other info, or an instance marked with what is happening? Doing karaoke, book club meeting, group game night, pool tournament, etc",
